        "original_id": "c14055f0-afd5-54cb-885e-83ea1f77fc2e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Archie Andrews, John L. Goldwater, Bob Montana, Vic Bloom, Fiona Staples, Mike Costa\n- Organizations: Archie Comics, WildStorm\n- Products: Archie (comic book), The Archie Show, Archie's Weird Mysteries, Archie Andrews (radio series), syndicated Archie comic strip, North 40, DV8: Gods and Monsters, T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents, Saga\n\nFacts:\n- Archie Andrews was created in 1941 by publisher John L. Goldwater and artist Bob Montana in collaboration with writer Vic Bloom.\n- Archie Andrews is the main character in an American comic book series published by Archie Comics.\n- Archie Andrews is also featured in the long-running Archie Andrews radio series, a syndicated comic strip, The Archie Show, and Archie's Weird Mysteries.\n- Archie is an ongoing comic book series featuring the Archie Comics character Archie Andrews.\n- Fiona Staples is a Canadian comic book artist known for North 40, DV8: Gods and Monsters, T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents, Archie, and Saga.\n- Mike Costa's first published work was a 2008 title created with artist Fiona Staples for WildStorm.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
